{
  "name": "Track Google keyword rankings in Google Sheets with drop alerts using API.SH",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track your Google rankings weekly and get alerted on drops\n\n### How it works\nEvery Monday this workflow reads your keywords from a Google Sheet, runs each one through Google search with the **API.SH** node, and finds where your domain ranks in the results (subdomains count). It logs the date, position, ranking URL and the domain in first place to a **History** tab, saves the latest position on the keyword row, and emails you once when keywords drop by your threshold or fall out of the results checked.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **API.SH** node (nodes panel → search \"API.SH\") and add your API key from [api.sh](https://api.sh). Every 10 results checked cost 1 credit per keyword (30 results = 3 credits); every account gets 1,000 free credits a month.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a **Keywords** tab (headers `keyword`, `last_position`, `last_url`, `last_checked`) and a **History** tab (headers `date`, `keyword`, `position`, `url`, `previous_position`, `change`, `top_result`).\n3. Paste the sheet URL into the three Google Sheets nodes and connect Google Sheets and Gmail.\n4. In **Settings**, set your domain, country, how many results to check and the alert threshold.\n\n### Customization\nRun it daily, add a `location` to the API.SH node for local rankings, or post the summary to Slack.",
